  "title": "Prehensions take time, so the felt now has thickness",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "7ca8de1c-4e4a-481e-943f-be46c954a513",
      "text": "Prehensions are not instantaneous but have temporal extent, which accounts for the temporality of experience: the now has a thickness, and a melody is heard as a sequence retained in the present, as in Husserl’s retention and protention.",
